---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import QualificationNotice from "../components/QualificationNotice.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Financial Services | BeaconGuard for Regulated Financial AI Actions"
  description="BeaconGuard independently authorizes AI provider invocation and declared financial actions. The AI result remains untrusted; analysts, models, and financial systems of record retain decision authority."
>
  <section class="stack-section industry-hero">
    <p class="section-label">FINANCIAL SERVICES WORKFLOWS</p>
    <h1>Govern financial AI actions before they execute.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      BeaconGuard independently authorizes AI provider invocation and declared
      financial actions. The returned AI result remains an untrusted proposal,
      while customer analysis, risk models, and financial systems of record
      retain decision authority.
    </p>

    <figure class="industry-diagram">
      <img
        src="/images/diagrams/industries/beaconguard-financial-governed-ai-transaction.png"
        alt="Financial governed AI transaction. A financial enterprise application prepares a governed request, Request Admission controls whether the AI provider may be invoked, the returned AI result remains untrusted, Result-to-Action controls the intended financial action, the enterprise application executes only an authorized action, the financial system of record remains authoritative, and both authorization decisions produce Verifiable Decision Records."
        width="1536"
        height="512"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>The financial authorization boundary</h2>
    <p>
      Request Admission DENY prevents provider invocation. Result-to-Action DENY
      prevents enterprise effect. Verify is read-only and cannot grant runtime
      permission.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Authorization scope</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        BeaconGuard authorizes whether the application may invoke the AI
        provider under the Active Verified Release.
      </li>
      <li>
        BeaconGuard authorizes whether a declared financial action based on an
        untrusted AI proposal may proceed — for example, a recommendation,
        escalation, communication, or case-state change.
      </li>
      <li>
        The financial application executes an authorized action. Systems of
        record remain authoritative.
      </li>
      <li>
        BeaconGuard does not determine fraud, AML, KYC, credit, dispute, or
        legal outcomes. Customer analysts, models, and systems of record retain
        those judgments.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Existing systems remain in place</h2>
    <p>
      BeaconGuard does not replace case management, transaction systems, analyst
      authorization, model risk management, or compliance judgment. BeaconGuard
      authorizes; the enterprise application executes.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>Financial action-control scenarios</h2>
    <p>
      Illustrative controlled examples. Each treats the AI result as an
      untrusted proposal whose declared use requires independent authorization.
    </p>
    <div class="scenario-grid">
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Route a case recommendation</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes a case recommendation.</li>
          <li>The application declares the intended disposition or queue action.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the application to proceed; DENY prevents enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          Case-management systems remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Escalate a fraud review</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes an escalation.</li>
          <li>The application declares the intended escalation route.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the application to proceed; DENY prevents enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          Case and escalation platforms remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Authorize customer communication</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes a customer-facing message.</li>
          <li>The application declares send, queue, or suppress.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the application to proceed; DENY prevents enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          Customer operations and compliance remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Control a case-state change</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes a case-status or ownership change.</li>
          <li>The application declares the intended state update.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the application to proceed; DENY prevents enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          Case management remains authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="scenario-card">
        <h3>Gate a dispute action</h3>
        <ul class="scenario-flow">
          <li>AI proposes an investigative or remediation action.</li>
          <li>The application declares the intended dispute workflow action.</li>
          <li>BeaconGuard evaluates the active controls.</li>
          <li>ALLOW permits the application to proceed; DENY prevents enterprise effect.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="scenario-authority">
          Fraud and dispute platforms remain authoritative.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stack-section">
    <h2>What BeaconGuard does not claim</h2>
    <ul class="bg-nonclaim-list">
      <li>Fraud, AML, KYC, credit, or legal determination</li>
      <li>Replacement of analyst authorization or compliance judgment</li>
      <li>Replacement of case management or transaction systems</li>
      <li>Model risk management certification</li>
      <li>Production-ready or customer financial production validation</li>
      <li>Semantic authorization of model content as truth</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <QualificationNotice variant="full" />

  <section class="stack-section">
    <div class="page-actions">
      <a
        class="btn-primary"
        href="mailto:architecture@beaconguardassurance.com?subject=Financial%20Workflow%20Review"
      >
        Request a Financial Workflow Review
      </a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/healthcare">Healthcare workflows</a>
      <a class="btn-secondary" href="/docs/architecture">Review System Architecture</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
